pkits/
    The NIST Public Key Interoperability Test Suite (PKITS), 2011 version:
    https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/PKI-Testing/documents/PKITS.pdf (the description) and
    https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/PKI-Testing/documents/PKITS_data.zip (the data), downloaded on
    2026-10-25.
    License: a work of the U.S. Government (NIST), not subject to copyright in the United States.
    Format: certs/ and crls/ are the DER certificates (.crt) and CRLs (.crl) of PKITS_data.zip, unchanged. cases.txt
    has one line per test or sub-test of section 4: number | title | OK or FAIL | settings | objects.
    - settings: "default" (the default settings of section 3), or a comma-separated list of explicit-policy,
      policy-set=OID,..., mapping-inhibit and any-inhibit (the initial-* inputs of RFC 5280 section 6.1.1);
    - objects: the files of certs/ and crls/ in the order of the test's "Certification Path", the trust anchor
      first and the end entity last.
    How cases.txt was made: PKITS.pdf was converted to text; each test's title, "Certification Path" list and
    "Expected Result" were extracted (the object names joined into file names), and the settings were taken from the
    procedure of each test of sections 4.8 to 4.12. Every row was then checked by hand against the PDF and against its
    title (Valid or Invalid). The first extraction misclassified six expectations, corrected from the PDF: the text
    "The path not should validate" (a typo of the PDF) in 4.4.20, 4.4.21 and 4.9.3, and conditional results in 4.12.x.
    Used: every test; 4.1.4 and 4.1.5 are skipped (DSA signatures). OpenSSL disagreements are discussed in
    .docs/cert.md.

limbo/
    x509-limbo (C2SP), https://github.com/C2SP/x509-limbo, commit 1080e565f26e544bbe9cf99953be8a57c08e7e20,
    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/C2SP/x509-limbo/main/limbo.json downloaded on 2026-10-25.
    License: Apache License 2.0 (limbo/LICENSE).
    Format: limbo.json is the suite's JSON (version 1): each test case has its trusted, untrusted and peer
    certificates (PEM), CRLs, validation time, expected result, purposes and expected peer name.
    How it was made: tools/limbo_subset.py keeps every case except those of bettertls::nameconstraints, of which it
    keeps every 16th (905 of 9802 cases); run it on the full limbo.json to remake the file. The tests run the full
    suite instead when UMILIB_LIMBO names its limbo.json.
    Used: every case of the file; the 13 that differ by design are listed with their reasons in
    tests/auth/cert/path.rs (LimboCase::DIVERGENCES).
